[{:db/id "q-83344/selection/b173c5a2261289451a16851a82385805247345a31f5bbe71acde4c5d6d00dd07" :answer/id #uuid "aa3e7705-7ef0-51d2-8802-8384517fffbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83344/selection/1d3bd5a6ab8849ce3b852e55e120c2c05cf35999908ac4706cd776a9f59ec079" :answer/id #uuid "9e8574b8-47bb-5131-8160-dba8654e1cdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{{s}^{2}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83344/selection/c71daaa02510bd00e19569ebc36b07be15c89c367cdef8e23bf4180865722f78" :answer/id #uuid "252a2822-33c9-5ec5-9a21-5fa03f0ec6f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{2{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83344/selection/35942ed4bc5248798cbd93d2340b3c5dd5ed2ab2130a38a0876b2fe78a0ea8fb" :answer/id #uuid "5387bf07-eb79-5513-b9fa-f101e0ece918" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83344/selection/dd45a193257740c84924c6e42f615129b027afb34e77e86ba22c2769a2bbd26d" :answer/id #uuid "5bc20064-ff9c-5942-92c9-2f180b317f4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2}{s({s}^{2}+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83344/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f9199ca-e0bd-53d4-a735-07e5a01345f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83344/selection/35942ed4bc5248798cbd93d2340b3c5dd5ed2ab2130a38a0876b2fe78a0ea8fb" :answer-field/choices ["q-83344/selection/b173c5a2261289451a16851a82385805247345a31f5bbe71acde4c5d6d00dd07" "q-83344/selection/1d3bd5a6ab8849ce3b852e55e120c2c05cf35999908ac4706cd776a9f59ec079" "q-83344/selection/c71daaa02510bd00e19569ebc36b07be15c89c367cdef8e23bf4180865722f78" "q-83344/selection/35942ed4bc5248798cbd93d2340b3c5dd5ed2ab2130a38a0876b2fe78a0ea8fb" "q-83344/selection/dd45a193257740c84924c6e42f615129b027afb34e77e86ba22c2769a2bbd26d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83344" :question/id #uuid "96144212-9114-5fc2-80e5-379d5ef7a54d" :question/math-academy-id "q-83344" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of $y(t),$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}} & =L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's introduce $L{y}=Y(s).$ \n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{″}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}Y(s).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}} & =L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83344/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4487c2b9-b681-5e1d-a2d9-c3231afcf03d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83344"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83349/selection/56531e0ce0b665de2130aae0a5d56de2443d5bdeea60626d423f62cd447b39a4" :answer/id #uuid "cb9e75e8-3857-56e5-8d92-963124d94993" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{(s+1)(s-2)}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83349/selection/41d0ac47d1a75aee9b79f95301375171861e83c6b864db873c509434c23efed3" :answer/id #uuid "76c7b1d3-3196-5efa-b944-5bfd9399805d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83349/selection/0bd93a9aca825ec3f69170dd67fc8b1470fb3e578b3ce799ddb4da4eff36a118" :answer/id #uuid "3537a214-54ac-5508-b261-a67bd8ee5fa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83349/selection/d318d69694bc080d5b3675ee31cdd6d8929585fe70b70a7eec03ce47db9cac49" :answer/id #uuid "5dfed2de-d2d4-56a2-8392-f8bcfd0dd828" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83349/selection/731b86d75dd781d7bb6268e9a036769d97db79f0d2c9a3d4e9ea619314bd196b" :answer/id #uuid "2d89d86d-3260-5175-b038-0aac6a3e7fae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83349/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90c8d0b3-6716-55bb-abfa-a2971aad16f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83349/selection/731b86d75dd781d7bb6268e9a036769d97db79f0d2c9a3d4e9ea619314bd196b" :answer-field/choices ["q-83349/selection/56531e0ce0b665de2130aae0a5d56de2443d5bdeea60626d423f62cd447b39a4" "q-83349/selection/41d0ac47d1a75aee9b79f95301375171861e83c6b864db873c509434c23efed3" "q-83349/selection/0bd93a9aca825ec3f69170dd67fc8b1470fb3e578b3ce799ddb4da4eff36a118" "q-83349/selection/d318d69694bc080d5b3675ee31cdd6d8929585fe70b70a7eec03ce47db9cac49" "q-83349/selection/731b86d75dd781d7bb6268e9a036769d97db79f0d2c9a3d4e9ea619314bd196b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83349" :question/id #uuid "a0460607-3703-5b65-ac28-ed82b0bd3298" :question/math-academy-id "q-83349" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of $y(t),$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=1,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{1} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's introduce $L{y}=Y(s).$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}}$ and $L{{y}^{″}},$  we use formulas for the Laplace transforms of the derivatives and apply the initial conditions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}} & =sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s) \\\\ L{{y}^{″}} & ={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =L{1} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s)-sY(s)-2Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s+1)(s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83349/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4487c2b9-b681-5e1d-a2d9-c3231afcf03d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83349"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102398/selection/a7d174a43390e09541800084b90f499be7d57a78c6b1ab86e4657dca19dcda86" :answer/id #uuid "c04cd324-9e95-5554-bf11-e55903676b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102398/selection/241bce79e45382f3be503fee63ac7429c6fe6a156d09967728bd9d1f404d4ec1" :answer/id #uuid "95e7c248-a15b-55c8-8fc0-4f045c4489d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{4}{(s+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102398/selection/f6685df4183816022c7602c277635757eb3e0f97f30229aa2c9d8544266df949" :answer/id #uuid "4e1846b0-62b0-5288-b131-39ca23c10dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102398/selection/6c70c8cd305f2ff9f00f8e8f126ddce6cc940f80efabdb9d9de2b7e9603f7f52" :answer/id #uuid "4a762cb4-97d3-560a-ac31-c6430a3b9c71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{2(s+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102398/selection/499e11f3c3fe33e991a4f0442ea1ed4309457764833a894572691edf7b0aff88" :answer/id #uuid "4a3db602-6a4b-5bd4-9960-37c91df76df1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{4(s-2)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102398/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "16296926-3c15-52aa-82c2-6ccf22944aee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102398/selection/a7d174a43390e09541800084b90f499be7d57a78c6b1ab86e4657dca19dcda86" :answer-field/choices ["q-102398/selection/a7d174a43390e09541800084b90f499be7d57a78c6b1ab86e4657dca19dcda86" "q-102398/selection/241bce79e45382f3be503fee63ac7429c6fe6a156d09967728bd9d1f404d4ec1" "q-102398/selection/f6685df4183816022c7602c277635757eb3e0f97f30229aa2c9d8544266df949" "q-102398/selection/6c70c8cd305f2ff9f00f8e8f126ddce6cc940f80efabdb9d9de2b7e9603f7f52" "q-102398/selection/499e11f3c3fe33e991a4f0442ea1ed4309457764833a894572691edf7b0aff88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102398" :question/id #uuid "176f4b0f-78af-5c61-b230-6d198c1455ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-102398" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of $y(t),$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4y={e}^{-t},\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-4y} & =L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-4L{y} & =L{{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's introduce $L{y}=Y(s).$ \n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{″}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}={s}^{2}Y(s)-1.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{-t}}=\\frac{1}{s+1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-4L{y} & =L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}Y(s)-1)-4Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-4)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1}+1 \\\\ ({s}^{2}-4)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{(s+1)({s}^{2}-4)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{(s+1)(s-2)(s+2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{(s+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102398/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4487c2b9-b681-5e1d-a2d9-c3231afcf03d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102398"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64442"] :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s\\ge \\sqrt{2}$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2y={t}^{2},\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-2y} & =L{{t}^{2}} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-2L{y} & =L{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{″}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}Y(s)-2.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-2L{y} & =L{{t}^{2}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}Y(s)-2)-2Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-2)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{3}+1)}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{3}+1)}{{s}^{3}({s}^{2}-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-83345/selection/396cc0966f0165b4a439c2ae156315ff0052523afb4a597d2c9f625ec36f3101" :answer/id #uuid "4eb7ea4a-3c91-598d-92f2-7e0564a1dc30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83345/selection/5b97546563ac351e81f14039e08d9d7cc0fc7f605593862cb195155706681fb0" :answer/id #uuid "126d70b3-1747-5e96-a336-264a3603113d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83345/selection/b3bc1232a9e6c7a1b1b1dde77938855c785de0b4aa7fbc2acfcf4bdca53e0a9f" :answer/id #uuid "ddf768b6-738e-5b1a-a0d9-1b875a9da90a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{3}+1}{{s}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83345/selection/712bd181c55607676f8512885554156133600fca0ab191edf640cc7340cabfaa" :answer/id #uuid "f6b0afe9-454a-5a1c-8631-627b90b2e99c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83345/selection/9105a63d151dc279f697f2402623547a22bed30302bff4495f8b5c0559e10850" :answer/id #uuid "cdbb5626-8023-5a6c-9f3e-d1f65a38cc5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{4}+1}{{s}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83345/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1f73d28-275e-5d7d-b0bf-bdcf83caf893" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83345/selection/396cc0966f0165b4a439c2ae156315ff0052523afb4a597d2c9f625ec36f3101" :answer-field/choices ["q-83345/selection/396cc0966f0165b4a439c2ae156315ff0052523afb4a597d2c9f625ec36f3101" "q-83345/selection/5b97546563ac351e81f14039e08d9d7cc0fc7f605593862cb195155706681fb0" "q-83345/selection/b3bc1232a9e6c7a1b1b1dde77938855c785de0b4aa7fbc2acfcf4bdca53e0a9f" "q-83345/selection/712bd181c55607676f8512885554156133600fca0ab191edf640cc7340cabfaa" "q-83345/selection/9105a63d151dc279f697f2402623547a22bed30302bff4495f8b5c0559e10850"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83345" :question/id #uuid "7d20a9b4-1729-5832-9ee1-d11c22dc11d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-83345" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of $y(t),$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=t,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}} & =L{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's introduce $L{y}=Y(s).$ \n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{″}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{′}(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}={s}^{2}Y(s)-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}} & =L{t} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s)-1 & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+1 \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83345/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4487c2b9-b681-5e1d-a2d9-c3231afcf03d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83345"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345083/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "17ca2126-31aa-5417-9046-fc4cf6e430e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345083/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "54204d03-1bb2-5f56-b7bb-bc580952fbf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345083/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-345083/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345083" :question/id #uuid "c5309c60-b128-5b86-8386-d3be90c807dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-345083" :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)+y(t)=7,\\,y(0)=7,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s)=\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s) & =\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{7}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>0.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{7}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =7{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345083/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d5c275-af4a-5bdd-a97c-c937824d8e94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345083"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345076/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "1a3a4f28-b93a-5069-b49f-3aa613d10094" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345076/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "7bc4ac5f-8ad9-54f0-8f98-608d1d8e3494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345076/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "208824f9-ba12-5238-a14d-93ae23ea0cc4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345076/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-345076/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-345076/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345076" :question/id #uuid "74a8f81e-ae52-5920-95ee-456b5a7bd468" :question/math-academy-id "q-345076" :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)-4y(t)=-4,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)-s-4Y(s)=-\\frac{4}{s}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-s-4Y(s) & =-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-4)Y(s) & =s-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-4)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{s({s}^{2}-4)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>2.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345076/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d5c275-af4a-5bdd-a97c-c937824d8e94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345084/field-1/b1745ed57f2f6e52f59a6eb2022eaec1c2a13d5bdb0d018886e0bdbc792bd87b" :answer/id #uuid "f2c2f855-54cc-5fe7-bff6-722f44637bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t^4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345084/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "76532c76-92fd-5b14-90d5-ad97b24000b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345084/field-1/b1745ed57f2f6e52f59a6eb2022eaec1c2a13d5bdb0d018886e0bdbc792bd87b" :answer-field/choices ["q-345084/field-1/b1745ed57f2f6e52f59a6eb2022eaec1c2a13d5bdb0d018886e0bdbc792bd87b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345084" :question/id #uuid "53011fc0-463a-5123-b45a-cadefcb42935" :question/math-academy-id "q-345084" :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)+y(t)=2{t}^{4}+24{t}^{2},\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s)=\\frac{48(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{5}}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s) & =\\frac{48(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{5}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{48(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{5}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{48}{{s}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>0.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{48}{{s}^{5}}} \\\\ y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}} \\\\ y(t) & =2{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345084/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d5c275-af4a-5bdd-a97c-c937824d8e94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345078/field-1/699bc7f77aa6ba0e4386391ce9b6d927d9a144ac144bba781e9fbe0bbb99778c" :answer/id #uuid "2b9ef45d-3bb0-5e09-8854-6a2c9d31f66e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-t}+e^{3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345078/field-1/168eb6974026cec80817b4b770b05778b771baba752e22c36c02fec29d94d0cd" :answer/id #uuid "6d02d649-29db-5cfc-9577-e75e23690bd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345078/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "89973892-42fe-5487-a484-8851acf3e058" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345078/field-1/699bc7f77aa6ba0e4386391ce9b6d927d9a144ac144bba781e9fbe0bbb99778c" :answer-field/choices ["q-345078/field-1/699bc7f77aa6ba0e4386391ce9b6d927d9a144ac144bba781e9fbe0bbb99778c" "q-345078/field-1/168eb6974026cec80817b4b770b05778b771baba752e22c36c02fec29d94d0cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345078" :question/id #uuid "8cde5879-da5e-5bfd-ad35-d1683362d0b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-345078" :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-9y=-8{e}^{-t},\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)-2s-2-9Y(s)=-\\frac{8}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-2s-2-9Y(s) & =-\\frac{8}{s+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-9)Y(s) & =2s+2-\\frac{8}{s+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-9)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+2s-3)}{s+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-9)Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s+3)(s-1)}{s+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s+3)(s-1)}{(s+1)(s-3)(s+3)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2(s-1)}{(s+1)(s-3)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>3.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}} \\\\ y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}} \\\\ y(t) & ={e}^{-t}+{e}^{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345078/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d5c275-af4a-5bdd-a97c-c937824d8e94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345078"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345071/field-1/362bede28713d3197ad64f218eaeca6d1a474cd0ab03423f4e1040470371e970" :answer/id #uuid "eb387394-b7c0-52bb-9a1b-1cd3a3fc488e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sin(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144407 :answer-field/correct "q-345071/field-1/362bede28713d3197ad64f218eaeca6d1a474cd0ab03423f4e1040470371e970" :answer-field/choices ["q-345071/field-1/362bede28713d3197ad64f218eaeca6d1a474cd0ab03423f4e1040470371e970"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-345071"] :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)-y(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)-1-Y(s)=-2(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}).\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-1-Y(s) & =-2(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\ ({s}^{2}-1)Y(s) & =1-\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-1)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>1.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6663"] :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y(t)\\right\\}$ for $s\\geq\\sqrt5$ if \n\n$$\ny'' - 5y = 4e^{-3t}, \\quad y(0)=2, \\quad y'(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-5y} & =L{4{e}^{-3t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-5L{y} & =4L{{e}^{-3t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y\\right\\}-sy(0)-y'(0)=s^2Y(s)-sy(0)-y'(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2Y(s)-2s+1.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{e^{-3t}\\right\\}=\\dfrac{1}{s+3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-5L{y} & =4L{{e}^{-3t}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}Y(s)-2s+1)-5Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{s+3} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{s+3}+2s-1 \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{4+(2s-1)(s+3)}{s+3} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+5s+1}{s+3} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+5s+1}{(s+3)({s}^{2}-5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6666"] :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ if the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\ny'' +  6y = 2\\sin {2t}, \\quad y(0) = 0, \\quad y'(0) = 2\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\ns^2Y(s) - 2 +6 Y(s)  =  2\\left(\\dfrac{2}{s^2 + 4}\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-2+6Y(s) & =2(\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}), \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+12}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+6)}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{Y(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y(t) =  \\sin {2t}$ is the solution of the original differential equation." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
